  "details": "Expression Parameter that is used by unused ExpressionMenu is assumed as used.\n**Steps to reproduce**\n1. Create two ExpressionMenu.\n2. Create one ExpressionParameters.\n3. Add \"ActuallyUsed\" parameter to the ExpressionParameters.\n4. Add control with \"FakelyUsed\" parameter to second ExpressionMenu.\n5. Add second ExpressionMenu as SubMenu of first ExpressionMenu\n6. Change type of control of SubMenu created in step 5 to something else (e.g. Button).\n7. Set first ExpressionMenu and the ExpressionParameters to some AvatarDescripter.\n8. Now, \"VRCExpressionMenu uses a parameter that is not defined. Parameter: FakelyUsed\" error occurs.\n**Details of bug**\nFixing either one of the following behavior should fix this problem.\n- When we changed type of control, `subMenu` field of Control is not cleared. If this is cleared, this problem will not happened.\n- In the `VRCSdkControlPanelAvatarBuilder3A.ValidateFeatures.FindParameters`, `subMenu` is always used to find SubMenus. If it check the type of control, this problem will not happened.",
